1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,667
Do. Home.

2
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:02,867
…Home it is.

3
00:00:02,867 --> 00:00:04,833
9 a.m., the living room.

4
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:07,233
It's fine. I'm using everything I bought.

5
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:10,633
Ten lanterns, one hammock, two tents.

6
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:12,667
Dad, our house turned into a forest!

7
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:14,600
Now, shall we light a fire?

8
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,467
Not in the house.

9
00:00:16,467 --> 00:00:19,567
Firewood confiscated. Electric grill instead.

10
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:22,533
Of five kilos of pork belly: four hundred grams.

11
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:25,433
Ah… so this is what lying horizontally feels like.

12
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:27,700
Mom: best weekend of her life.

13
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,133
But what about the frogs?

14
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:30,933
Ribbit. Ribbit ribbit.

15
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:33,900
Dad became a frog. Voluntarily.

16
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,200
Dad, make a dinosaur shadow!

17
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,067
A dinosaur! …No, that's a chicken.

18
00:00:39,067 --> 00:00:41,733
Next morning. Campsite weather: sunny.

19
00:00:41,733 --> 00:00:42,733
…Whyyyy!

20
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:44,033
We can go next week.

21
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:45,933
Living-room camping again next week!

22
00:00:45,933 --> 00:00:48,300
Ding. Installment one of twelve, paid.

23
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:50,767
The other eleven, at the next fork in the road.

24
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:53,733
Curious about the other ending? Press Mo.
